  "notes": "National Industrialization Company (Tasnee; ticker 2060) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/386_0_2026-03-16...). Auditor PwC. Board of Directors approved the consolidated financial statements on 12 March 2026 (Note 49). The five primary statements (printed pages 7-11) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.5x); the notes are digital text. Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). The FY2024 comparatives are restated (issuer Notes 45 and 46 - the 2024 SAMCO business combination). FY2025 was a heavy LOSS year: a SAR 2,108.1m impairment of non-financial assets and a SAR 821.7m share of losses from associates/JVs drove an operating loss of SAR 3,359.3m, partly offset by a SAR 2,029.0m net gain on debt restructuring; net loss SAR 1,466.2m, of which SAR 1,765.3m was attributable to the parent's shareholders (NCI took a SAR 299.1m profit). retained_earnings fell to SAR 1,030.1m. Tasnee is classifying a disposal group (its titanium-dioxide / Cristal-related assets, note 46) as held for sale - assets_held_for_sale SAR 1,102.3m, liabilities_held_for_sale SAR 388.7m - presented outside the current / non-current subtotals, so noncurrent_assets / noncurrent_liabilities are NOT carried (total would not tie to current + non-current within tolerance) and the balance-sheet check runs on total_assets = total_liabilities + total_equity. IFRS 5: income_before_income_taxes_and_zakat is NOT carried (the reported 'Loss before zakat and income tax from continuing operations' is a continuing-operations figure); continuing_operations_income and discontinued_operations_income are carried and net_income = continuing + discontinued is checked. income_taxes_and_zakat is the reported 'Zakat and income tax' (continuing operations). operating_income is the reported 'Operating loss' (Tasnee presents the share of associates'/JVs' results and asset impairments ABOVE operating loss). other_nonoperating_income is the 'Gain on debt restructuring, net' one-off. impairment_charges is the 'Impairment of non-financial assets' P&L line. other_reserves combines the statutory reserve and the negative 'Other reserves'. long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current 'Long-term borrowings' and its current portion; IFRS 16 lease liabilities are mapped separately. defined_benefit_obligation is the non-current 'Employee benefits obligations'. investments_associates is 'Investments in equity accounted associates and joint ventures'. depreciation_amortization sums 'Depreciation and amortization' and 'Right-of-use assets depreciation' from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Additions to property, plant and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Finance costs paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'. No ordinary dividend to the parent's shareholders (subsidiaries paid SAR 250,688 thousand to NCI). The balance-sheet 'Cash and bank balances' (2,018,200) differs from the cash-flow closing balance (2,144,524, which includes SAR 126,324 thousand of cash inside the held-for-sale disposal group and excludes restricted cash) so the cash-to-balance-sheet cross-check warns - expected. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: financial position 7, profit or loss 8, changes in equity 10, cash flows 11.",
